ISSUE TITLE: Compression dictionary training fails with "insufficient samples" on large-chunk tables (SSTableChunkSampler per-SSTable allocation rounds to zero)
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
h2. Summary

{{nodetool compressiondictionary train}} fails with {{Insufficient samples for training: N (minimum required: 11)}} on tables that have a large {{chunk_length_in_kb}} and many SSTables, even when there are gigabytes of data available to sample.
h2. Root cause

{{SSTableChunkSampler}} ({_}src/java/org/apache/cassandra/db/compression/SSTableChunkSampler.java{_}) allocates the number of chunks to sample from each SSTable using integer division that truncates to zero for most SSTables when the sample target is small.

{{{}calculateTargetChunkCount(){}}}:
{code:java}
int averageChunkSize = totalDataSize / totalChunks;      // ~ chunk_length_in_kb
return config.maxTotalSampleSize / averageChunkSize;     // target shrinks as chunk size grows
{code}
With the default {{maxTotalSampleSize = 8 MiB}} and 64 KiB chunks: {{{}targetChunkCount = 8 MiB / 64 KiB = 128{}}}.

{{{}sampleChunksFromSSTables(){}}}:
{code:java}
long chunksFromThisSSTable = Math.min((targetChunkCount * info.chunkCount) / totalChunks, remainingTarget);
if (chunksFromThisSSTable <= 0)
    continue;   // <-- SSTable skipped entirely
{code}
{{(targetChunkCount * info.chunkCount) / totalChunks}} 

